(357861, 27872, 5728, '<td valign="top">And another ribbon makes 6! Congrats Crab, you deserved it.</td>', 'And another ribbon makes 6! Congrats Crab, you deserved it.', '2003-07-16 03:49:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(357866, 27921, 5728, '<td valign="top">YAYAYA you got it Nyki, way to go! And you see a "firework" photo even took a ribbon. Met the challenge wonderfully. Go and celebrate now :-)</td>', 'YAYAYA you got it Nyki, way to go! And you see a "firework" photo even took a ribbon. Met the challenge wonderfully. Go and celebrate now :-)', '2003-07-16 03:52:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(357940, 27750, 8298, '<td valign="top">Hurray! I was half drunk when i took this shot. Under normal circumstances I''d probably not even get a ribbon! Thank you all for your very insightful and extremely helpful suggestions and encouragement. As my first entry, i really didn''t know what to expect, but you''ve all be very supportive and positive.<br/> <br/>I can''t stress enough the power of the Canon S30. I took this shot 2 days after purchasing it used online. I''ve always had a fetish for perspective, unique angle, and clear focus. Definitely had to use a tripod for this shot. <br/> <br/>The S30 naturally produces a star filter effect for all long exposures (sorry S30 owners, I let the secret out), great bonus for the camera. The amber lighting really made for mellow mood and sleepy tone. I was happy for the fact that there were many complimentary lines to use for a great depth effect. I personally like how the rail tries desperately to contain the light from the lamps.<br/> <br/>A few people suggested cropping out the boat, and i partially agree with them. Others found the boat a positive compositional element giving broader subject range.. and i partially agree with them too. Others prefered adding people on the promenade in order to fit the theme of the challenge, but i felt it''d be too distracting. The promenade works best as a complete and intact subject. I also feel that adding people would throw the composition off balance and would saturate the picture with too many visual elements. But they were all valid suggestions and i thank them for it.<br/> <br/>My trusty little optex tripod has a level bubble indicating flat and level footing. This helped immeasuably.<br/> <br/>Thank you all for the very kind feedback! good luck with your Round submissions!</td>', 'Hurray! I was half drunk when i took this shot. Under normal circumstances I''d probably not even get a ribbon! Thank you all for your very insightful and extremely helpful suggestions and encouragement. As my first entry, i really didn''t know what to expect, but you''ve all be very supportive and positive. I can''t stress enough the power of the Canon S30. I took this shot 2 days after purchasing it used online. I''ve always had a fetish for perspective, unique angle, and clear focus. Definitely had to use a tripod for this shot.  The S30 naturally produces a star filter effect for all long exposures (sorry S30 owners, I let the secret out), great bonus for the camera. The amber lighting really made for mellow mood and sleepy tone. I was happy for the fact that there were many complimentary lines to use for a great depth effect. I personally like how the rail tries desperately to contain the light from the lamps. A few people suggested cropping out the boat, and i partially agree with them. Others found the boat a positive compositional element giving broader subject range.. and i partially agree with them too. Others prefered adding people on the promenade in order to fit the theme of the challenge, but i felt it''d be too distracting. The promenade works best as a complete and intact subject. I also feel that adding people would throw the composition off balance and would saturate the picture with too many visual elements. But they were all valid suggestions and i thank them for it. My trusty little optex tripod has a level bubble indicating flat and level footing. This helped immeasuably. Thank you all for the very kind feedback! good luck with your Round submissions!', '2003-07-16 05:27:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(357943, 27750, 8843, '<td valign="top">ahhaha are you sugguesting we should all get half drunk to take pictures? ;P Congrats roley! ;P</td>', 'ahhaha are you sugguesting we should all get half drunk to take pictures? ;P Congrats roley! ;P', '2003-07-16 05:30:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(358057, 27710, 9765, '<td valign="top">Great shot. I live in Florida USA but was there back in September of last year. My girlfriend lives there and I went to visit her then. She will be moving here to US in June of next year and I can''t wait. Anyway it was nice to see a photo of the city. As soon as I saw it I knew it was HK even before I read the description hehehe. I know this is your home and you see photos of it all the time but if you are interested in seeing through another set of eyes please look at these from last year when I was there.  <a href="//www.pbase.com/tomh1000/hong_kong" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">//www.pbase.com/tomh1000/hong_kong</a> Best of luck to you and your family.<br/> <br/>Tom</td>', 'Great shot. I live in Florida USA but was there back in September of last year. My girlfriend lives there and I went to visit her then. She will be moving here to US in June of next year and I can''t wait. Anyway it was nice to see a photo of the city. As soon as I saw it I knew it was HK even before I read the description hehehe. I know this is your home and you see photos of it all the time but if you are interested in seeing through another set of eyes please look at these from last year when I was there.  //www.pbase.com/tomh1000/hong_kong Best of luck to you and your family. Tom', '2003-07-16 07:20:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(358061, 27602, 8406, '<td valign="top">thanx a lot guys, i''m not photographer... but i''ll be some day =)<br/>thanx for ou criticize. i''ll do a better job next time ;)</td>', 'thanx a lot guys, i''m not photographer... but i''ll be some day =)thanx for ou criticize. i''ll do a better job next time ;)', '2003-07-16 07:23:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(358075, 27710, 5624, '<td valign="top">what''s up doc??? wow! nice job landing at 9th... i know you''ll make it at top 10... i really love the colors... <br/> <br/>:-)</td>', 'what''s up doc??? wow! nice job landing at 9th... i know you''ll make it at top 10... i really love the colors...  :-)', '2003-07-16 07:37:57.000000', NULL, 0),
