(368970, 27882, 5222, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by andrewlr:</b></div><hr/><i>This shot is a great depiction of a "night on the town".  I like the fast paced action feel that you get with the motion blur.  Beautiful colour tones as well.  I''d have liked the image a bit bigger though. Hope this does well.  Good luck!</i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Cheers for the comment Andrew. <br/>I dont know why i didn''t enter the full size version? <br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2003-07-28 18:29:53.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by andrewlr:This shot is a great depiction of a "night on the town".  I like the fast paced action feel that you get with the motion blur.  Beautiful colour tones as well.  I''d have liked the image a bit bigger though. Hope this does well.  Good luck!  Cheers for the comment Andrew. I dont know why i didn''t enter the full size version? ', '2003-07-28 19:22:38.000000', '2003-07-28 19:29:53.000000', 0),
(368973, 27882, 5222, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by bryskyd:</b></div><hr/><i>This would have been a much better photo on a time-lapse tripod, so the background would be in focus... 4</i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Did you read my description? I was in a moving car going along a uneven road. The distorted image comp is what i was after.<br/> <br/>If I wanted to capture the detail of the buildings in the background, I would of stopped the car and yes used a tripod.</td>', 'Originally posted by bryskyd:This would have been a much better photo on a time-lapse tripod, so the background would be in focus... 4  Did you read my description? I was in a moving car going along a uneven road. The distorted image comp is what i was after. If I wanted to capture the detail of the buildings in the background, I would of stopped the car and yes used a tripod.', '2003-07-28 19:27:35.000000', NULL, 0),
